course: dictionary
lesson: 13490
title: Ignition: the moment things catch fire
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Ignition has more than one meaning, and the words around it tell you which one you need. Read the whole sentence before you decide. «Dad turned the key in the ignition, and the engine roared.» Here ignition is the switch that starts the car.
explain: «The dry leaves caught fire at the moment of ignition.» Here ignition is the moment something starts to burn. Ask yourself: what is happening in the sentence? Fire is starting, so ignition must be the start of the burning.
explain: In science, ignition is the start of burning in an engine or rocket when fuel is lit. «At ignition, the rocket engines lit, and then it lifted off the pad.» The rocket is taking off, so ignition is the start of that burning.
fact: Ignition means the moment something catches fire or starts burning.
fact: The ignition in a car is the switch you turn with a key or a button to start the engine.
fact: A fire needs three things: fuel, heat and oxygen. This is called the fire triangle.
fact: In a rocket launch, the countdown ends with «ignition!» and then «lift-off».
fact: Useful phrases: «turn the key in the ignition», «point of ignition», «ignition key».
exercise: «Dad turned the key in the ignition, and the engine roared.» What is the ignition here? | *The switch that starts the engine | The seat belt | The lights on the dashboard | The tyres of the car
exercise: «The dry leaves caught fire at the moment of ignition.» What does ignition mean? | A kind of fire alarm | The end of a fire | A cold, wet day | *The moment something starts to burn
exercise: In the fire triangle, which three things must meet for a fire to start? | Sun, rain and snow | *Fuel, heat and oxygen | Water, sand and wind | Paper, glue and string
test: «At ignition, the rocket engines lit, and then it lifted off the pad.» In this sentence, ignition means | A kind of rocket fuel | *The start of burning in the rocket engines | The view from the sky | The end of the countdown with no fire
test: Which phrase means the key that starts a car? | *Ignition key | Fire key | Lift-off key | Spark key
exam: «The point of ignition was the moment the match touched the oily rag.» What does point of ignition mean? | Where the fire was put out | *The moment the fire began | The shop where the match was sold | The colour of the oily rag
